// ZULRAH'S GRAPHICS, and which attack each one belongs to.
//
// OSRS gives this snake exactly four spot animations, 1044 to 1047, and nothing else in the whole
// 4,023-record table shares its palette: a scan of every OSRS spotanim for a recolour whose targets
// are Zulrah's dark green (HSL hue 29 - 30608 and 30236) finds 1044 and 1045 and no third. So the
// block is the fight's, entire, and the only question was which of the four is which.
//
// THE LAST ROUND GOT IT WRONG BY ONE, and the owner saw it: "the venom clouds are showing as
// fireballs". 1046 was taken for the cloud and drawn on the ground every tick - and 1046 is
// model 26593, whose 266 faces are yellow (hue 10) and orange (hue 4) and whose own recolour
// (5060->4025, 11185->6067, 11200->7097) maps orange onto DARKER ORANGE. It is a fireball. It was
// never a cloud. Rendering the four re-encoded meshes side by side (tools/models/ob2render.py) is
// what showed it: three green-and-white comets and one ball of flame.
//
// SO WHAT IS EACH? The cache says what they look like and the wiki says what Zulrah throws:
//
//   1044  model 20390, ONE dark-green orb with a tail, seq 5358 which LOOPS 8 times
//   1045  model 11221, TWO of that same orb (277 faces to 20390's 139, the same three colours),
//         seq 3151 which does not loop
//   1046  model 26593, the ball of flame, resized to 96 and lit at ambient 60
//   1047  model 20390 again, recoloured white (HSL 127 is lightness 127 at zero saturation)
//
// and the strategy page says Zulrah "will spawn venomous clouds during the fight via a BARRAGE of
// dark-green orbs" and summons snakelings "via shooting WHITE orbs". A barrage is more than one
// orb, and 1045 is literally two of them; a white orb is 1047 and there is only one white one. That
// leaves 1044, the single green orb that loops while it flies, for the ranged attack, and 1046 for
// the magic attack - which is the assignment the private-server community publishes for this snake
// as well (range 1044, toxic cloud 1045, mage 1046, snakeling 1047; rune-server thread "Zulrah
// Animation/GFX Ids"). Cache and community agree, so that is what is wired below.
//
// THE MODELS WERE ALREADY RIGHT. All four .ob2 files were byte-identical to the cache's models
// re-encoded with their own spotanim recolours baked in - md5 for md5 - so nothing was re-imported
// this round. Only the names were wrong, and the names are what the scripts read, so the names
// moved: model.pack 24254-24257 and spotanim.pack 1280-1283 keep their ids and carry new ones.
//
// AND A FIFTH, BECAUSE FOUR WAS NOT ENOUGH. Everything above is last round's reasoning and it
// still holds for 1044, 1046 and 1047. What it got wrong was giving 1045 two jobs: the orbs that
// FLY to a tile and the cloud that then LIES on it. Those are not the same graphic and 1045 is
// only ever the first of them - see [zulrah_venom_cloud] below for what the cloud is now and how
// certain that is.
//
// Imported by tools/models/importosrsspot.py; models re-encoded by osrs2ob2.py, animations
// converted by animconvosrs.py.

[zulrah_ranged]
// OSRS spotanim 1044 - the ranged attack, and the green form's whole repertoire. One dark-green
// orb that spins its way to you.
model=spot_zulrah_ranged
anim=zulrah_orb_spin
ambient=20

[zulrah_magic]
// OSRS spotanim 1046 - the magic attack. It really is a ball of fire; the last round's mistake was
// putting it on the floor, not importing it.
model=spot_zulrah_magic
anim=zulrah_magic_spin
resizeh=96
resizev=96
ambient=60

[zulrah_venom_orbs]
// OSRS spotanim 1045 - the venom BARRAGE, in flight and nothing else. TWO of 1044's orb in one
// mesh (277 faces to 20390's 139, the same three colours, the same 4665 rig, the same green
// recolour), which is what makes a "barrage of dark-green orbs" a barrage.
model=spot_zulrah_venom
anim=zulrah_venom_orb_spin
ambient=30

[zulrah_venom_cloud]
// OSRS spotanim 1043 - the cloud that LIES ON THE GROUND, which until this round was 1045 above.
//
// WHY IT COULD NOT GO ON BEING 1045. The owner's words were "the venom clouds ... just dont appear
// to have the correct model", and the cache says why in one line: 1045 is 1044's comet, doubled.
// Same frame group (4665), same seq family (3151 is the non-looping half of 5358), same green
// recolour, and a mesh that is literally two copies of the single orb. Rendering all four of
// Zulrah's spotanims side by side (tools/models/ob2render.py through the spot renderer) shows three
// green comets and one fireball and nothing that could be a cloud. What was on the floor for
// twenty-five ticks was two projectiles lying in the grass.
//
// WHAT 1043 IS, AND HOW SURE THIS IS. Model 29421 is a ragged green gas puff - 572 faces of hue-40
// green, no tail, no direction - and its only other users in the whole table are two recolours of
// itself (2599 into blues, 3486 flattened to one colour at 70%), which is the shape of a shared
// gas-cloud graphic. It sits immediately below Zulrah's own block, and its model id is in the same
// 26000-29000 band as 1046, the one graphic that was modelled new for this snake, rather than in
// the 20390/11221 band of the three that were reused.
//
// THAT IS A REASONED PICK, NOT A PROVEN ONE. A modern cache holds no script that would say "Zulrah
// spawns graphic N", so nothing here can prove 1043 is the id Old School uses; what it can prove is
// that 1045 is a projectile and therefore is not the cloud. If this one is wrong it is wrong in the
// direction of a green gas cloud instead of a green gas cloud.
//
// AND IT IS SCALED WIDE AND FLAT, which no other graphic in this file is, and the numbers were
// picked by looking at it in the client rather than by arithmetic. The mesh is 42 units across and
// 74 deep - a third of a tile - and one of these has to read as the 3x3 that ^zulrah_cloud_radius
// damages. resizeh 512 is the most the config allows - SpotAnimConfig.ts refuses anything over it -
// and is four times across, so a cloud is about a tile and a third wide and two and a half deep;
// resizev 170 is only a third again as tall, so it LIES on the platform instead of standing on it.
// Four times is not nine, so one puff does not blanket its whole 3x3; several of them landing side
// by side is what covers the platform, which is also what a barrage of them looks like in Old
// School - scattered blobs with gaps, not a carpet.
//
// The first cut of this was 384 and 256 with the old cloud's ambient=30 still on it, and the frames
// out of javaclient/tools/clienttests/run_zulrahshots.py showed why that is wrong: nine bright mint
// lumps standing up off the floor, which read as gemstones and not as gas. The ambient is gone -
// OSRS spotanim 1043 carries none, and the 30 was inherited from the graphic this replaced - and
// with it the glow.
// AND IT IS RECOLOURED DOWN, which is the one thing here that is not the cache's and the one thing
// the first set of frames out of the client insisted on. Model 29421 has exactly six colours and
// they are bright: the 308 faces that make up most of it are hue 20 at lightness 64, the highlights
// go to 88, and fourteen faces are hue 53, a cyan. On a dark platform that draws as nine glowing
// mint GEMSTONES lying in a row - which is what the shots showed, and it is not what venom looks
// like. The six pairs below are the same six colours at hue 24-30 and lightness 22-51: still green,
// still unmistakable, but a murky swamp green in the family of Zulrah's own (the snake's greens are
// hue 29 at lightness 16-28) rather than a lit crystal.
//
// The values are RGB15 because that is what the packer takes - SpotAnimConfig.ts runs every recol
// through ColorConversion.rgb15toHsl16 - so the sources are the RGB15 that converts to each of the
// model's stored HSL16 colours, not those colours themselves.
// THE MESH IS THE MOLE MUD CLOUD, RECOLOURED. OSRS 1043 was a reasoned pick and it was wrong:
// rendered through tools/models/ob2render.py it is a bright, spiky, six-colour crystal - the
// owner's screenshot of green gemstones lying on the platform is exactly what that model is.
//
// spot_mole_mud_cloud_spotanim is a billowing cloud silhouette, 264 vertices of ONE colour
// (hsl16 7700, a dark brown), which is what makes this a single recolour pair rather than six.
// It was chosen by rendering every cloud-ish graphic in the build side by side - the smoke puffs
// are a single teardrop, smoke_barrage_impact is scattered particles, dustdevil_dust is three
// spheres - and it is the only one shaped like a cloud.
//
// 8386 is the RGB15 that converts to the brown the model stores; 2473 converts to hue 28,
// saturation 5, lightness 30 - a dark swamp green in the family of Zulrah's own (hue 29 at 16-28)
// rather than a lit crystal. Not every HSL has an RGB15 that converts to it, which is why the
// value is this one and not a rounder number.
//
// No ambient: the last mesh inherited ambient=30 and glowed. A cloud on a dark platform should
// not be the brightest thing on it.
model=spot_mole_mud_cloud_spotanim
anim=zulrah_venom_cloud
// SIZE, THIRD ATTEMPT. 512/170 was the old crystal mesh, which was tiny. 320/140 on THIS mesh
// came back "too large" from the owner - the clouds merged into one carpet across the platform,
// where Old School has scattered blobs with gaps between them. 160/120 is half the width again.
//
// 128 is 100%, so this is a quarter again over the mesh as drawn rather than two and a half
// times it. The damage is still the 3x3 ^zulrah_cloud_radius covers whatever the graphic does -
// a cloud you can see the edges of is the point, not one that hides the platform.
resizeh=160
resizev=120
recol1s=8386
recol1d=2473
[zulrah_snakeling_orb]
// OSRS spotanim 1047 - the white orb that puts a snakeling on the floor beside you.
model=spot_zulrah_snakeling_orb
anim=zulrah_orb_spin
ambient=20
